    lines += ["","### Disposition totals for the separate 30-label domain summary","","| Disposition | Count |","|---|---:|"]
    for key,val in sorted(d["disposition_counts_for_30_domain_summary_labels"].items()): lines.append(f"| `{key}` | {val} |")
    lines += ["","### Complete item-level triage","","Each row preserves the exact inventory label and frequency metadata. Frequency is not evidence of commonness across the domain; ‘possible area support’ is conditional and not a route mapping.","","| # | Inventory label | Owner/visibility flag | n (metadata only) | Disposition | Possible area support |","|---:|---|---|---:|---|---|"]
    for i,item in enumerate(d["legacy_skill_dispositions"],1):
        sup = "; ".join(item["possible_area_support_if_task_fits"]) or "none established"
        vis = (item["canonical_owner_flag"] or "unmarked")+" / "+(item["canonical_visibility_flag"] or "unmarked")
        lines.append(f"| {i} | {item['canonical_label']} | {vis} | {item['role_aggregate_count_metadata_only']} | `{item['disposition']}` | {sup} |")
    lines += ["","## Domain summary inventory dispositions","","| # | Exact label | n metadata | Disposition | Possible area support |","|---:|---|---:|---|---|"]
    for i,item in enumerate(d["domain_structure_summary_dispositions"],1):
        lines.append(f"| {i} | {item['canonical_label']} | {item['role_aggregate_count_metadata_only']} | `{item['disposition']}` | {'; '.join(item['possible_area_support_if_task_fits']) or 'none established'} |")
    lines += ["","## Candidate item decisions","","The item records in the companion JSON contain the full per-item contract: identity, plain-language explanation, practical use, checkpoint, evidence locators, global/Nigeria scope, status, expected output, relationships/prerequisites, verified learning link and limitations. Items whose exact method tutorial was not verified are held and intentionally have no student link.",""]
    for item in d["candidate_items"]:
        lines += [f"### {item['label']}","",f"- **Disposition/status:** `{item['disposition']}` / `{item['status']}`",f"- **Learner explanation:** {item['meaning']}",f"- **Expected output:** {item['output']}",f"- **Possible area support:** {', '.join(item['areas']) if item['areas'] else 'none established'}",f"- **Evidence locators:** "+"; ".join(f"{x['source_id']}: {x['exact_locator']}" for x in item['evidence']),f"- **Learning links:** "+"; ".join(f"[{x['label']}]({x['url']}) (level: {x['level']}; access: {x['access']}; language: {x['language']}; duration: {x['duration']}; checked {x['verified_on']})" for x in item['learning_links']),f"- **Relationships/prerequisites:** "+("; ".join(x['type']+" → "+x['target']+": "+x['note'] for x in item['relationships']) or "No prerequisite asserted."),f"- **Limits/scope:** "+"; ".join(item['limits'])+" "+item['scope'],""]
    lines += ["## Computation, methods and alternatives","","Computational and quantitative social research is a recognized specialist path, supported by UC San Diego, Cornell's named method examples and the existing D078 method inventory. That evidence does **not** make coding, statistics, network analysis, text mining, computational models or GIS common requirements for every D078 learner. Keep a non-computational path available. Select one method/tool only when it fits the question, data and ethical permissions. Specific sequence/text/model methods stay held unless their individual identity, task fit and direct learning link are verified. The JSON records the seven method entries, including duplicate social-network analysis and the inaccessible ASA PDF source.","","A tool is not a method: KoboToolbox can deploy a form but does not validate sampling; Taguette can organise text codes but does not validate interpretation; Gephi can visualize ties but does not prove influence; QGIS can analyse mapped data but only helps where place matters; Jamovi/R/Python support different workflows and are alternatives where the task supports them.","","## Certifications and qualifications","","No universal professional certification is established. NHREC/TRREE ethics training is conditional to specified Nigeria health-research/ethics-review contexts. KoboToolbox Essentials gives its own product-course certificate; it is not a social-science professional qualification. Do not turn either into a blanket D078 requirement. No common entry qualification is established by the reviewed sources.","","## Evidence register","","The companion JSON contains the same source register with exact locators, scope and claim limits. Direct learner links are also listed per candidate item.",""]
    for source in d["source_register"]:
        lines.append(f"- **{source['id']} — {source['publisher']}, _{source['title']}_** ([source]({source['url']})); locator: {source['locator']} Scope/limit: {source['scope']}; {source['limits']}")
    lines += ["","## Unresolved items and next gate","","- Observation/ethnography and the computational method umbrella have no sufficiently direct, method-specific beginner learning link verified; keep both hidden until individually resolved.","- A broad, current Nigerian employment/work-setting or demand study was not established; do not add labour-market, salary or licensing claims.","- The D078 overview gate is not passed. The programme overview and pre-domain-entry reviews remain prior dependencies in the implementation plan.","- The research candidates should be reconciled against exact checkpoint claims, display language and resource-link requirements before any promotion.","- This review makes no role fit, role placement or area/role assignment decision.","","## Generation and validation","",f"This artifact was generated from read-only local inputs by `data/career-mapping/_audit/build_d078_full_domain_item_inventory_2026_10_08.py`. Validation: all 137 provenance labels and all 30 domain-summary labels have explicit dispositions; no unmatched labels; every displayable detailed candidate has a direct learning link; held methods are explicitly unlinked; no role records opened; no student approval asserted.",""]
    OUT_MD.write_text("\n".join(lines),encoding="utf-8")

